tal Statistics System (NVSS) birth data.\"}]}, {\"v\": \"before/after or trend\", \"ev\": [{\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"From 2012 to 2016, the standardized prevalence of gestational diabetes increased from 5.2% to 5.6%.\"}]}], \"methods_quotes\": [{\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"Crude prevalences were calculated overall and by selected maternal characteristics among women with complete information for each particular characteristic\"}, {\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"chi-square tests were used to evaluate differences by characteristic\"}, {\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"directly standardizing to the distribution of age and race/ethnicity of U.S. resident mothers with live births in 2012\"}, {\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"differences were assumed to be independent and were evaluated using the z-statistic\"}, {\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"P-values <0.05 were considered statistically significant.\"}], \"confidence\": \"high\", \"uncertain_fields\": [\"study_design\"]}", "type": "text"}]}